<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Map of the quantum world | Quantum Research Center</title><meta name="description" content="Explore a network of quantum mechanics, computing, information, communication, matter, and technology topics."><link rel="icon" href="../icons/icon.svg"><script src="../education/computing/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="../navigation.js"></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="map.css"><script defer src="map.js"></script></head>
<body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="news-toolbar"><!-- NAV --></header>
<main id="main" tabindex="-1"><header class="map-intro"><div><p class="kicker">An atlas of connected ideas</p><h1>The quantum world</h1><p>Follow a thread. Discover how the ideas connect.</p></div><span id="map-count" class="map-count"></span></header>
<div class="workspace"><aside class="explorer" aria-label="Explore topics"><label for="search">Find a quantum idea</label><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Try entanglement, qubits, spin…" autocomplete="off"><label for="branch">Explore a field</label><select id="branch"><option value="">All fields</option></select><label for="depth">Level of detail</label><select id="depth"><option value="3">All keywords</option><option value="2">Fields &amp; subfields</option><option value="1">Main fields</option></select><p id="results-status" role="status"></p><div id="results" class="results" aria-label="Matching topics"></div><div class="legend"><p class="kicker">Fields of study</p><div id="legend"></div></div><details class="directory"><summary>Browse the topic directory</summary><p>Available with or without JavaScript.</p><!-- DIRECTORY --></details></aside>
<section class="graph-panel" aria-label="Interactive topic network"><div class="graph-heading"><span>Knowledge graph</span><span>Parent → child</span></div><canvas id="graph" tabindex="0" aria-label="Quantum topic graph. Drag to pan, scroll to zoom. Use arrow keys to pan, plus and minus to zoom. Use the topic directory or search to select topics."></canvas><div class="graph-controls"><button id="zoom-in" aria-label="Zoom in" type="button">+</button><button id="zoom-out" aria-label="Zoom out" type="button">−</button><button id="fit" type="button">Fit graph</button></div><p class="graph-help">Drag to explore · Scroll to zoom · Select a node</p></section>
<aside id="detail" class="detail" aria-label="Selected topic" aria-live="polite"></aside></div>
<p class="map-note">A growing, curated map of quantum science. Connections organize broader topics into narrower topics; they are not prerequisites or an exhaustive account of every relationship. Browse the directory for a text alternative.</p><noscript><p class="map-note">Enable JavaScript for the interactive graph. All keywords are available in the topic directory above.</p></noscript></main><!-- DATA --></body></html>
